{"pageProps":{"sections":[{"id":"copilot_your_partner","title":"Describe it. Review it. Ship it.","description":"Copilot in the editor helps you build both AI and non-AI integrations from natural language. Ask it to generate a service, map data between types, answer questions about Ballerina, or draft tests, then review and edit the code it produces like any other code.","details":"Copilot is a WSO2 Integrator capability (platform-specific) available in VS Code. Its slash commands include `/ask`, `/doc`, `/openapi`, `/typecreator`, and `/data-map`, and it can generate tests and restore earlier checkpoints. Generated code is a starting point: compile it, test it, and review it before it reaches production.","links":[{"label":"Copilot capabilities (WSO2 Integrator documentation)","url":"https://wso2.com/integration-platform/docs/develop/copilot/copilot-capabilities","action":"Read the documentation"},{"label":"AI-generated test cases (WSO2 Integrator documentation)","url":"https://wso2.com/integration-platform/docs/develop/test/ai-generated-cases","action":"Read the documentation"},{"label":"WSO2 Integrator extension for VS Code","url":"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=WSO2.wso2-integrator","action":"Get the extension"}],"tabs":[{"key":"codegen","title":"Code generation","src":"/images/ai_codegen.png","alt":"VS Code with the WSO2 Copilot panel: the prompt \"Write a todo http service\" and the generated Ballerina HTTP service with CRUD resources for todos.","width":2758,"height":1874,"code":""},{"key":"datamapper","title":"AI data mapper","src":"/images/ai_datamapper.png","alt":"The Ballerina data mapper next to the WSO2 Copilot panel, where a data-mapping request for a transform function produced mappings from a DetailedPerson record to a DetailedStudent record.","width":2758,"height":1874,"code":""},{"key":"ask","title":"Ask","src":"/images/ai_ask.png","alt":"The WSO2 Copilot panel answering \"/ask Explain the isolated concept\" with an explanation and reference links to Ballerina by Example pages.","width":2758,"height":1874,"code":""},{"key":"tests","title":"Test generation","src":"/images/ai_test.png","alt":"The WSO2 Copilot panel generating a test plan and Ballerina test functions for a todo HTTP service.","width":2758,"height":1874,"code":""}]},{"id":"natural-programming-vs-code-features","title":"Requirements in. Code out. Drift caught.","description":"Keep requirements, code, and documentation in sync. Generate an implementation and tests from high-level business requirements, then check later changes for drift between what the requirements say and what the code does.","details":"Requirements-to-code and drift detection are offered through Copilot's `/natural-programming` command, which the WSO2 Integrator documentation labels **experimental** (platform-specific). Drift checks use a model at development time, so treat each finding as a suggestion to review, not as proof that the code matches or violates a requirement. Tests generated from requirements give you a repeatable check that does not depend on the model.","links":[{"label":"Copilot capabilities: /natural-programming (WSO2 Integrator documentation)","url":"https://wso2.com/integration-platform/docs/develop/copilot/copilot-capabilities","action":"Read the documentation"},{"label":"Introducing natural programming (blog)","url":"https://blog.ballerina.io/posts/2025-04-26-introducing-natural-programming/","action":"Read the post"}],"tabs":[{"key":"requirements","title":"Code from requirements","src":"/images/np_code_generation_from_requirements.png","alt":"Copilot receiving claim management requirements through the experimental /natural-programming command and generating a Ballerina expense-claims service.","width":1414,"height":809,"code":""},{"key":"drift","title":"Drift detection and fixes","src":"/images/np_drift_check.gif","alt":"Animation of a drift check in VS Code underlining code in an expense-claims service that no longer matches the requirements.","width":656,"height":654,"code":""},{"key":"tests","title":"Tests from requirements","src":"/images/np_test_generation_from_requirements.png","alt":"Copilot receiving \"/natural-programming (experimental) Generate tests against the requirements\" and producing a test plan and Ballerina tests for claim submission and status retrieval.","width":2829,"height":1616,"code":""}]},{"id":"natural-programming-complie-time-code-generation","title":"Prompts at build time. Plain Ballerina at run time.","description":"Generate code from a prompt while the project compiles. Annotate an external function with `@natural:code` to have the compiler generate its body, or use a `const natural` expression to generate typed constant data, such as realistic test fixtures.","details":"Compile-time code generation is an **experimental** language feature, introduced in Ballerina 2201.13.0 and still available in 2201.14.0 through the `ballerina/ai.np` compiler extension. Builds need the `--experimental` flag and a code-generation service configured through the `BAL_CODEGEN_URL` and `BAL_CODEGEN_TOKEN` environment variables, which the VS Code command **Ballerina: Configure default WSO2 model provider** sets up (platform-specific). The model runs during the build, not when the program runs. Review and test the generated code as you would any other code. This is different from [runtime natural expressions](/use-cases/ai/#natural-expressions), which call a model each time the program runs.","links":[{"label":"Release notes: compile-time code generation (2201.13.0)","url":"/downloads/swan-lake-release-notes/swan-lake-2201.13.0/#compile-time-code-generation","action":"Read the release notes"},{"label":"ballerina/ai.np API documentation","url":"https://lib.ballerina.io/ballerina/ai.np/latest/","action":"View the API docs"},{"label":"Filter products using compile-time code generation","url":"https://github.com/ballerina-guides/ai-samples/tree/main/filter-products-using-compile-time-code-generation","action":""}],"tabs":[{"key":"function","title":"Generated function body","src":"","alt":"","width":0,"height":0,"code":"<pre class=\"shiki github-light\" style=\"background-color:#fff;color:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><button type=\"button\" title=\"Copy\" aria-label=\"Copy\" data=\"import ballerina/http;\n\npublic type Product record {|\n    string id;\n    decimal price;\n|};\n\nfinal Product[] productCatalog = [\n    {id: &#x22;PROD001&#x22;, price: 999.99},\n    {id: &#x22;PROD002&#x22;, price: 699.99},\n    {id: &#x22;PROD003&#x22;, price: 29.99},\n    {id: &#x22;PROD004&#x22;, price: 19.99},\n    {id: &#x22;PROD005&#x22;, price: 49.99}\n];\n\nfunction filterProductsAbovePrice(Product[] products, decimal priceThreshold) returns Product[] = @natural:code {\n    prompt: &#x22;Filter products that have a price greater than the given price threshold.&#x22;\n} external;\n\nservice / on new http:Listener(8080) {\n    resource function get products/filter(decimal minPrice) returns Product[]|http:BadRequest {\n        return filterProductsAbovePrice(productCatalog, minPrice);\n    }\n}\" class=\"rehype-pretty-copy\" onclick=\"navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.attributes.data.value);this.classList.add(&#x27;rehype-pretty-copied&#x27;);this.setAttribute(&#x27;title&#x27;, &#x27;Copied&#x27;);this.setAttribute(&#x27;aria-label&#x27;, &#x27;Copied&#x27;);window.setTimeout(() => {this.classList.remove(&#x27;rehype-pretty-copied&#x27;);this.setAttribute(&#x27;title&#x27;, &#x27;Copy&#x27;);this.setAttribute(&#x27;aria-label&#x27;, &#x27;Copy&#x27;);}, 3000);\"><span class=\"ready\"></span><span class=\"success\"></span></button><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">import</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\"> ballerina/http;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">public</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\"> type</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1\"> Product</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\"> record</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\"> {</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">|</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5\">    string</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\"> id;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#005CC5\">    decimal</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\"> price;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">|</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">};</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">final</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\"> Product[] productCatalog </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">=</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\"> [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E\">    {id</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">:</span><span style=\"color:#032F62\"> \"PROD001\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">, price</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">:</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5\"> 999.99</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">},</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E\">    {id</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">:</span><span style=\"color:#032F62\"> \"PROD002\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">, price</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">:</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5\"> 699.99</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">},</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E\">    {id</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">:</span><span style=\"color:#032F62\"> \"PROD003\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">, price</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">:</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5\"> 29.99</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">},</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E\">    {id</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">:</span><span style=\"color:#032F62\"> \"PROD004\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">, price</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49\">:</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5\"> 19.99</span><span style=\"color:#24292E\">},</span></span>\n<span clas